= Pulse — Simple =

A '''pulse''' is a rhythmic wave you can often feel at places such as your wrist or neck when your heart pumps blood.

Counting pulse beats for one minute can estimate the heart's rate. A pulse also has a rhythm: beats may occur regularly or irregularly.

Pulse is not the same measurement as [[Blood pressure|blood pressure]]. The number can change with exercise, rest, stress, medicines and many other factors. A single count by itself cannot diagnose a health condition.

